# Valgrind suppressions for the Ghoti.io Model test suite.
#
# Add to this file only for allocations that are demonstrably not ours, and
# name the frames narrowly enough that a leak of our own cannot match. Every
# entry should say what it is, why it cannot be fixed here, and how it was
# shown to be narrow.

# glibc keeps one allocation for the LOCPATH search list, built in
# __argz_add_sep while newlocale() resolves a locale name. freelocale() does
# not release it, and the numeric-locale tests cannot avoid LOCPATH: this
# machine ships no comma-decimal locale, so the test generates one with
# localedef and LOCPATH is the only way to reach it.
#
# The three named frames are glibc's locale-path parsing, which nothing in
# this library calls. Shown to be narrow rather than assumed: with a
# deliberate 1234-byte leak planted in the test, valgrind still reported it
# while this entry suppressed the glibc one. The same check was done for
# LeakSanitizer, whose equivalent suppression lives in test_locale.cpp.
{
   glibc-newlocale-locpath-argz
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:realloc
   fun:argz_add_sep
   fun:newlocale
}
